+-2. Serve an OpenAI-compatible teacher. For the historical teacher, install vLLM separately and run `vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B --revision c202236235762e1c871ad0ccb60c8ee5ba337b9a --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8001 --language-model-only --default-chat-template-kwargs '{"enable_thinking": false}'`. Select quantization and hardware settings appropriate to the host.
++2. Serve an OpenAI-compatible teacher. For the historical teacher, install vLLM separately and run `vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B --revision c202236235762e1c871ad0ccb60c8ee5ba337b9a --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8001 --language-model-only --default-chat-template-kwargs '{"enable_thinking": false}'`. Select quantization and hardware settings appropriate to the host. On a host too small for vLLM, `just teacher-gguf` serves a quantized GGUF through `llama-server` on the same upstream port, using the Vulkan build from `devenv.nix`. Its settings are `TEACHER_GGUF`, `TEACHER_GGUF_CONTEXT`, `TEACHER_GGUF_SLOTS` and `TEACHER_GGUF_GPU_LAYERS`. A GGUF teacher is a different model and serving stack from the historical one, so record its file hash in `TEACHER_MODEL_REVISION`, set `CONCURRENCY` to at most its slot count, re-pass the headroom gate and do not compare its results directly with other teachers.
+ 3. Run `just teacher`, then verify its health and authenticated generation. Set the teacher review identifier and credentials as needed.
